{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01XzijRND9HH2Wxnkt63BjhB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Translation contract (READ FIRST)\n2\t\n3\tWe are translating the zstd C library (in `c_src/`) to Rust, file by file, into\n4\t`src/`. The result is a `cdylib` that must export the **same symbols** and\n5\tproduce **byte-identical output** as the C build.\n6\t\n7\t## Golden rules\n8\t\n9\t1. **Transliterate, do not redesign.** Mirror the C control flow, the C\n10\t   arithmetic, the C order of operations and the C order of error checks\n11\t   *exactly*. Do NOT fix bugs. Do NOT \"improve\" anything.\n12\t2. Use **raw pointers** (`*const u8`, `*mut u32`, ...) and `unsafe` blocks so\n13\t   pointer arithmetic matches C. Do not try to use slices/iterators for the\n14\t   hot paths that do pointer arithmetic.\n15\t3. Keep **C identifiers verbatim** (`ZSTD_compressBlock_fast`, `nbSeq`, `ip`,\n16\t   `oend`, ...). Lints for naming are already disabled crate-wide.\n17\t4. **Arithmetic must wrap, never panic.** The release profile has\n18\t   `overflow-checks = false`, but be explicit where C relies on wrapping:\n19\t   use `wrapping_add/sub/mul`, and `x as i32 as u32`-style casts to mirror C\n20\t   integer conversions. Signed/unsigned conversions must match C semantics\n21\t   (C `(U32)someNegativeInt` == Rust `x as u32`).\n22\t5. For pointer subtraction that may go before the start of a buffer (common in\n23\t   zstd, e.g. `iend - 8` when the buffer is shorter), use\n24\t   `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add`/`wrapping_offset` rather than `sub`/`add`.\n25\t6. `assert()` is compiled out (DEBUGLEVEL == 0) — **drop all asserts**.\n26\t   `DEBUGLOG`/`RAWLOG`/`ZSTD_STATIC_ASSERT`/`DEBUG_STATIC_ASSERT` — drop them.\n27\t   `ZSTD_TRACE` is 0, so all `ZSTD_trace*` calls compile out.\n28\t7. Build-time configuration for this port (**already decided, do not deviate**):\n29\t   - `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT = 5`  (so `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT >= 1..5` are true,\n30\t     `>= 6`/`>= 7`/`>= 8` are false; legacy v01..v04 *source files* are still\n31\t     compiled and still export their symbols)\n32\t   - `XXH_NAMESPACE = ZSTD_`\n33\t   - `DYNAMIC_BMI2 = 0`, `STATIC_BMI2 = 0`  → always take the \"default\"\n34\t     (non-bmi2) code path; keep the `bmi2`/`flags` parameters in signatures but\n35\t     ignore them, exactly like the C does when `DYNAMIC_BMI2 == 0`.\n36\t   - `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD` is **not** defined → single-threaded `POOL_*` stubs,\n37\t     `ZSTDMT_*` compiles its non-thread paths.\n38\t   - `DEBUGLEVEL = 0`, `NDEBUG`, no `ZSTD_TRACE`, no\n39\t     `ZSTD_STRIP_ERROR_STRINGS`, no `HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X1/X2`,\n40\t     no `ZSTD_NO_INTRINSICS`, no `ZSTD_LINUX_KERNEL`.\n41\t   - Target is x86_64 linux (little endian, 64-bit): `MEM_64bits()==1`,\n42\t     `MEM_isLittleEndian()==1`.\n43\t   - `ZSTD_ARCH_X86_SSE2` is **not** used for `ZSTD_copy16` (gcc path uses the\n44\t     `copy16_buf` memcpy pair) — but any of these produce identical bytes.\n45\t8. **Exported symbols**: every function that the C library exports must be\n46\t   ```rust\n47\t   #[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n48\t   pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn NAME(...) -> ... { }\n49\t   ```\n50\t   with the **final linker name** (e.g. legacy files use macros that rename\n51\t   `FSE_decompress` to `FSEv05_decompress`; use the renamed name).\n52\t   `static`/internal C functions become plain (non-`no_mangle`) Rust `unsafe fn`.\n53\t   Do NOT add `no_mangle` to functions that C declared `static`.\n54\t9. Structs shared across translation units, or reachable from the public API,\n55\t   must be `#[repr(C)]`.\n56\t10. Allocation must go through libc so behaviour matches:\n57\t    `crate::libc::{malloc, calloc, free, memcpy, memmove, memset, qsort, qsort_r}`\n58\t    and the helpers `crate::libc::{ZSTD_memcpy, ZSTD_memmove, ZSTD_memset}`.\n59\t    **`qsort`/`qsort_r` must be libc's** so tie-breaking matches byte-for-byte.\n60\t11. Prefer `while` loops over `for` when translating C `for` loops with\n61\t    non-trivial increments/continues, so `continue` semantics stay correct.\n62\t    Remember: C `continue` in a `for` loop still runs the increment; Rust's does\n63\t    not.\n64\t\n65\t## Existing shared modules (use these, don't re-create them)\n66\t\n67\t| Rust path | C origin | provides |\n68\t|---|---|---|\n69\t| `crate::libc` | `zstd_deps.h` | malloc/calloc/free/memcpy/memmove/memset/memcmp/qsort/qsort_r, `ZSTD_memcpy`, `ZSTD_memmove`, `ZSTD_memset` |\n70\t| `crate::zstd_h` | `zstd.h` | all public types/enums/constants (`ZSTD_customMem`, `ZSTD_bounds`, `ZSTD_Sequence`, `ZSTD_compressionParameters`, `ZSTD_parameters`, `ZSTD_frameParameters`, `ZSTD_FrameHeader`, `ZSTD_inBuffer`, `ZSTD_outBuffer`, `ZSTD_frameProgression`, `ZSTD_strategy`, `ZSTD_cParameter`, `ZSTD_dParameter`, `ZSTD_ResetDirective`, `ZSTD_EndDirective`, `ZSTD_dictContentType_e`, `ZSTD_dictLoadMethod_e`, `ZSTD_format_e`, `ZSTD_ParamSwitch_e`, `ZSTD_dictAttachPref_e`, `ZSTD_literalCompressionMode_e`, `ZSTD_forceIgnoreChecksum_e`, `ZSTD_refMultipleDDicts_e`, `ZSTD_SequenceFormat_e`, `ZSTD_FrameType_e`, `ZSTD_nextInputType_e`, `ZSTD_sequenceProducer_F`, `ZSTD_VERSION_*`, `ZSTD_MAGIC*`, `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`, `ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_*`, ...) |\n71\t| `crate::common::mem` | `mem.h` | `BYTE,U8,S8,U16,S16,U32,S32,U64,S64`, `MEM_read*/MEM_write*/MEM_readLE*/MEM_writeLE*/MEM_readBE*/MEM_writeBE*`, `MEM_32bits`, `MEM_64bits`, `MEM_isLittleEndian`, `MEM_swap*` |\n72\t| `crate::common::bits` | `bits.h` | `ZSTD_highbit32`, `ZSTD_countLeadingZeros32/64`, `ZSTD_countTrailingZeros32/64`, `ZSTD_NbCommonBytes`, `ZSTD_rotateRight_U16/32/64` |\n73\t| `crate::common::error_private` | `error_private.h`, `zstd_errors.h` | `ERROR(ZSTD_error_xxx)` (const fn), `ERR_isError`, `ERR_getErrorCode`, `ERR_getErrorName`, `ERR_getErrorString`, and every `ZSTD_error_*` constant |\n74\t| `crate::common::bitstream` | `bitstream.h` | `BIT_CStream_t`, `BIT_DStream_t`, `BIT_DStream_status` (+ `BIT_DStream_unfinished/endOfBuffer/completed/overflow`), `BIT_init*`, `BIT_addBits*`, `BIT_flushBits*`, `BIT_closeCStream`, `BIT_lookBits*`, `BIT_readBits*`, `BIT_skipBits`, `BIT_reloadDStream*`, `BIT_endOfDStream`, `BIT_mask`, `STREAM_ACCUMULATOR_MIN*`, `BitContainerType` |\n75\t| `crate::common::fse` | `fse.h` | `FSE_CTable`, `FSE_DTable`, `FSE_CState_t`, `FSE_DState_t`, `FSE_symbolCompressionTransform`, `FSE_DTableHeader`, `FSE_decode_t`, `FSE_repeat*`, all `FSE_*_SIZE*` helpers, `FSE_initCState`, `FSE_initCState2`, `FSE_encodeSymbol`, `FSE_flushCState`, `FSE_getMaxNbBits`, `FSE_bitCost`, `FSE_initDState`, `FSE_peekSymbol`, `FSE_updateState`, `FSE_decodeSymbol`, `FSE_decodeSymbolFast`, `FSE_endOfDState`, `FSE_MAX_*`, `FSE_MIN_TABLELOG`, `FSE_TABLESTEP` |\n76\t| `crate::common::huf` | `huf.h` | `HUF_CElt`, `HUF_DTable`, `HUF_CTableHeader`, `HUF_repeat*`, `HUF_flags_*`, `HUF_TABLELOG_*`, `HUF_SYMBOLVALUE_MAX`, `HUF_*_WORKSPACE_SIZE*`, `HUF_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`, `HUF_CTABLE_SIZE*`, `HUF_DTABLE_SIZE`, `HUF_COMPRESSBOUND`, `HUF_BLOCKBOUND` |\n77\t| `crate::common::zstd_internal` | `zstd_internal.h`, `allocations.h` | `MIN`, `MAX`, `BOUNDED`, `ZSTD_OPT_NUM`, `ZSTD_REP_NUM`, `repStartValue`, `BIT0..BIT7`, `ZSTD_fcs_fieldSize`, `ZSTD_did_fieldSize`, `ZSTD_FRAMEIDSIZE`, `ZSTD_BLOCKHEADERSIZE`, `ZSTD_blockHeaderSize`, `blockType_e` (`bt_raw`/`bt_rle`/`bt_compressed`/`bt_reserved`), `ZSTD_FRAMECHECKSUMSIZE`, `MIN_CBLOCK_SIZE`, `MIN_SEQUENCES_SIZE`, `MIN_LITERALS_FOR_4_STREAMS`, `SymbolEncodingType_e` (`set_basic`/`set_rle`/`set_compressed`/`set_repeat`), `LONGNBSEQ`, `MINMATCH`, `Litbits`, `LitHufLog`, `MaxLit`, `MaxML`, `MaxLL`, `MaxOff`, `DefaultMaxOff`, `MaxSeq`, `MLFSELog`, `LLFSELog`, `OffFSELog`, `MaxFSELog`, `MaxMLBits`, `MaxLLBits`, `ZSTD_MAX_HUF_HEADER_SIZE`, `ZSTD_MAX_FSE_HEADERS_SIZE`, `LL_bits`, `LL_defaultNorm`, `LL_defaultNormLog`, `LL_DEFAULTNORMLOG`, `ML_bits`, `ML_defaultNorm`, `ML_defaultNormLog`, `ML_DEFAULTNORMLOG`, `OF_defaultNorm`, `OF_defaultNormLog`, `OF_DEFAULTNORMLOG`, `ZSTD_copy8`, `ZSTD_copy16`, `WILDCOPY_OVERLENGTH`, `WILDCOPY_VECLEN`, `ZSTD_overlap_e` (`ZSTD_no_overlap`/`ZSTD_overlap_src_before_dst`), `ZSTD_wildcopy`, `ZSTD_limitCopy`, `ZSTD_WORKSPACETOOLARGE_FACTOR`, `ZSTD_WORKSPACETOOLARGE_MAXDURATION`, `ZSTD_bufferMode_e`, `ZSTD_frameSizeInfo`, `blockProperties_t`, `ZSTD_defaultCMem`, `ZSTD_customMalloc`, `ZSTD_customCalloc`, `ZSTD_customFree`. It also re-exports everything from `crate::zstd_h`. |\n78\t| `crate::common::pool` | `pool.c/h` | `POOL_ctx`, `POOL_function`, `POOL_create`, `POOL_create_advanced`, `POOL_free`, `POOL_joinJobs`, `POOL_resize`, `POOL_add`, `POOL_tryAdd`, `POOL_sizeof` |\n79\t| `crate::common::xxhash` | `xxhash.*` | `XXH32_state_t`, `XXH64_state_t`, `XXH32_canonical_t`, `XXH64_canonical_t`, `XXH_errorcode`, `XXH_OK`, and the exported `ZSTD_XXH*` functions (call them by their `ZSTD_XXH64_*` names) |\n80\t| `crate::common::entropy_common` | `entropy_common.c` | `FSE_versionNumber`, `FSE_isError`, `FSE_getErrorName`, `HUF_isError`, `HUF_getErrorName`, `FSE_readNCount`, `FSE_readNCount_bmi2`, `HUF_readStats`, `HUF_readStats_wksp` |\n81\t| `crate::common::fse_decompress` | `fse_decompress.c` | `FSE_buildDTable_wksp`, `FSE_buildDTable_internal`, `FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2` |\n82\t\n83\tNote: `ZSTD_isError` / `FSE_isError` / `HUF_isError` used *inline* inside C code\n84\tare macros for `ERR_isError`. Prefer\n85\t`crate::common::error_private::ERR_isError(x) != 0`.\n86\t\n87\t## Idioms\n88\t\n89\t```rust\n90\t// C: RETURN_ERROR_IF(cond, dstSize_tooSmall, \"...\");\n91\tif cond { return ERROR(ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall); }\n92\t\n93\t// C: FORWARD_IF_ERROR(f(...), \"\");\n94\t{ let err_code = f(...); if ERR_isError(err_code) != 0 { return err_code; } }\n95\t\n96\t// C: CHECK_F(f(...));\n97\t{ let e = f(...); if ERR_isError(e) != 0 { return e; } }\n98\t\n99\t// C: size_t const x = ...;  ->  let x: usize = ...;\n100\t// C: BYTE* op = (BYTE*)dst;  ->  let mut op = dst as *mut BYTE;\n101\t// C: op[3]                   ->  *op.add(3)\n102\t// C: *op++ = v;              ->  *op = v; op = op.add(1);\n103\t// C: (size_t)(op - ostart)   ->  op.offset_from(ostart) as usize\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\tFor a C `static const` lookup table use a Rust `static NAME: [T; N] = [...];`.\n107\t\n108\tFor C unions or nested anonymous structs, use `#[repr(C)]` structs; if a real\n109\tunion is needed use `#[repr(C)] union`.\n110\t\n111\t## Deliverable\n112\t\n113\tWrite the assigned Rust file(s) completely — **no `todo!()`, no stubs, no\n114\t\"... rest omitted\"**. Every function in the assigned C file must be present.\n115\tDo not edit anything under `c_src/`. Do not edit `src/lib.rs` unless told to.\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Pv81pnpsdDh1B7AHmkDfhY","session_id":"91081e33-7aae-4a44-80fe-383759459deb","uuid":"c8dc1054-675d-4612-a621-42a9b0aa3056","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:26:53.704Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate legacy zstd_v01"}
