sBlock_fast\n  ZSTD_compressBlock_fast_dictMatchState\n  ZSTD_compressBlock_fast_extDict\n  ZSTD_fillHashTable\n\n`src/compress/zstd_double_fast.rs` must export exactly these 4:\n  ZSTD_compressBlock_doubleFast\n  ZSTD_compressBlock_doubleFast_dictMatchState\n  ZSTD_compressBlock_doubleFast_extDict\n  ZSTD_fillDoubleHashTable\n\nEverything else in those C files was `static`/`FORCE_INLINE_TEMPLATE` → private.\n\nImportant notes:\n - The C uses `FORCE_INLINE_TEMPLATE` generic functions parameterised on `mls`\n   (and `hasStep`, `dictMode`) with explicit dispatch switches at the bottom\n   (e.g. `ZSTD_COMPRESSBLOCK_FAST` style switch on `ms->cParams.minMatch`).\n   Translate the generic bodies as ordinary private `unsafe fn` taking the same\n   parameters, and reproduce the dispatch switches exactly.\n - `ZSTD_ROW_HASH_*` / row match finder is NOT in these files.\n - `ZSTD_DOUBLE_FAST` in zstd_double_fast.c is guarded by\n   `#ifndef ZSTD_EXCLUDE_DFAST_BLOCK_COMPRESSOR` — that macro is NOT defined, so\n   translate the whole file.\n   Likewise no `ZSTD_EXCLUDE_*` macro is defined anywhere in this build.\n - Pointer arithmetic that can go before a buffer start must use\n   `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_offset`.\n - assert()/DEBUGLOG are compiled out.\n - Reproduce integer truncations exactly, e.g. `(U32)(ip - base)`.\n\nSTEP 4 — Run `./check.sh compress/zstd_fast compress/zstd_double_fast` and\niterate until zero errors (warnings fine).\n\nSTEP 5 — Verify with\n  grep -o 'extern \"C\" fn [A-Za-z0-9_]*' src/compress/zstd_fast.rs | sed 's/.*fn //' | sort\n  grep -o 'extern \"C\" fn [A-Za-z0-9_]*' src/compress/zstd_double_fast.rs | sed 's/.*fn //' | sort\n\nRules: never modify anything under c_src/. Only create/modify the two files\nlisted in STEP 3. No stubs, no todo!(), no omitted functions.\n\nReport: line counts, step-5 output, and that check.sh passed.","uuid":"d132ea5f-1f6f-44b5-bd28-28685fd3a413","session_id":"91081e33-7aae-4a44-80fe-383759459deb"}
