{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hvtpejtzaxkfnmew5arrj34tqyxkq44v5ull3pup4gidregylcyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`src/legacy/zstd_v04.rs` is complete and verified.\n\n## What was done\n\nTranslated the whole 3598-line `c_src/src/legacy/zstd_v04.c` into one self-contained Rust module at `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-SxLoMM/translated_rust/src/legacy/zstd_v04.rs` (**3843 lines**). No other file was touched.\n\nEverything that was `static` in the C file became a private Rust `unsafe fn` inside this module — its own `mem.h` helpers, `BIT_*` bitstream, `FSE_*` decoder (`FSE_readNCount`, `FSE_buildDTable{,_raw,_rle}`, `FSE_decompress*`), `HUF_*` X2/X4 decoders (`HUF_readStats`, `HUF_readDTableX2/X4`, `HUF_fillDTableX4{,Level2}`, the `algoTime` selector table), the v0.4 block/sequence decoder, and the `ZBUFF_*` streaming layer. No shared `crate::common::*` module is used; only `crate::libc` for malloc/free/memcpy/memmove/memset, plus an `extern \"C\"` declaration of `ERR_getErrorString` (which is a genuine cross-TU call in the C too — `ERR_getErrorName`/`ERR_isError`/`ERROR` are re-implemented locally as the C header's `ERR_STATIC` inlines).\n\nBuild-config decisions applied per CONTRACT: `MEM_64bits()==1` / little-endian paths, the statically-false `MEM_32bits()` guards kept as no-op `if`s, the static `FSE_MAX_TABLELOG*2+7 > 64` reload tests preserved as dead const conditions, `DEBUGLOG` dropped. Wrapping arithmetic (`wrapping_add/sub/mul/shl/shr`, `wrapping_offset`) is used throughout for pointer walks that legally go out of bounds (`oend-8`, `iend-5`, `pEnd-7`, …) and for shifts with data-dependent amounts, so nothing can panic.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `./check.sh legacy/zstd_v04` → `Finished dev profile` — **zero errors, zero warnings**.\n- Step-5 grep output — all 17 required names, and exactly 17 `pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn` in the file:\n\n```\nZBUFFv04_createDCtx            ZSTDv04_createDCtx\nZBUFFv04_decompressContinue    ZSTDv04_decompress\nZBUFFv04_decompressInit        ZSTDv04_decompressContinue\nZBUFFv04_decompressWithDictionary  ZSTDv04_decompressDCtx\nZBUFFv04_freeDCtx              ZSTDv04_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy\nZBUFFv04_getErrorName          ZSTDv04_freeDCtx\nZBUFFv04_isError               ZSTDv04_nextSrcSizeToDecompress\nZBUFFv04_recommendedDInSize    ZSTDv04_resetDCtx\nZBUFFv04_recommendedDOutSize\n```\n\n- `nm` on the built rlib confirms those 17 as `T` symbols with the exact linker names, and nothing else from this file is exported. `ZSTDv04_isError` is indeed absent from the C source (only declared in the header), so it is not defined here — matching `SYMBOLS_BY_FILE.txt`.\n\n## Two notes worth flagging\n\n- **Switch fall-through**: `ZBUFF_decompressContinue` and `ZSTD_decompressContinue` rely on C `case` fall-through. I reproduced this with a labeled block (`'sw: { … break 'sw }`) plus a local `stage` variable that is advanced to the next case on fall-through, so the `loadHeader→decodeHeader→read→load→flush` chain and every mid-case `break` behave exactly as in C.\n- **`match` on `blockType_t`**: the C `switch` arms use lowercase constants (`bt_compressed`, …). Since a silent misread as pattern *bindings* would have made the first arm match everything, I verified the resolution with a standalone `rustc` test — it prints `100 101 102 103 999`, confirming they compile as constant patterns."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":215866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1099,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01R5KsGPJKy9MJPR6zX7zzst","session_id":"91081e33-7aae-4a44-80fe-383759459deb","uuid":"8c942c57-36d9-486c-984d-fb271aaba053","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:51:08.062Z","subagent_type":"gene