hat were `static`, they must be private to your module.\n119\t\n120\t## Verifying your work\n121\t\n122\t`./check.sh <module> [<module> ...]` type-checks the named modules together with\n123\tthe stable core, in a throw-away crate, so other people's in-progress files\n124\tcan't break your build. Module paths are relative to `src/` without `.rs`,\n125\te.g. `./check.sh compress/zstd_fast`.\n126\t\n127\t## Idioms\n128\t\n129\t```rust\n130\t// C: RETURN_ERROR_IF(cond, dstSize_tooSmall, \"...\");\n131\tif cond { return ERROR(ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall); }\n132\t\n133\t// C: FORWARD_IF_ERROR(f(...), \"\");\n134\t{ let err_code = f(...); if ERR_isError(err_code) != 0 { return err_code; } }\n135\t\n136\t// C: CHECK_F(f(...));\n137\t{ let e = f(...); if ERR_isError(e) != 0 { return e; } }\n138\t\n139\t// C: size_t const x = ...;  ->  let x: usize = ...;\n140\t// C: BYTE* op = (BYTE*)dst;  ->  let mut op = dst as *mut BYTE;\n141\t// C: op[3]                   ->  *op.add(3)\n142\t// C: *op++ = v;              ->  *op = v; op = op.add(1);\n143\t// C: (size_t)(op - ostart)   ->  op.offset_from(ostart) as usize\n144\t```\n145\t\n146\tFor a C `static const` lookup table use a Rust `static NAME: [T; N] = [...];`.\n147\t\n148\tFor C unions or nested anonymous structs, use `#[repr(C)]` structs; if a real\n149\tunion is needed use `#[repr(C)] union`.\n150\t\n151\t## Deliverable\n152\t\n153\tWrite the assigned Rust file(s) completely — **no `todo!()`, no stubs, no\n154\t\"... rest omitted\"**. Every function in the assigned C file must be present.\n155\tDo not edit anything under `c_src/`. Do not edit `src/lib.rs` unless told to.\n156\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01P1HmnrABH9LhuQAWoQYkSA","session_id":"91081e33-7aae-4a44-80fe-383759459deb","uuid":"53c419e0-f69e-43d9-b457-1e8a3ffd31c9","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:53:17.133Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate zstd_lazy"}
