{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01As2e7SneFq4GvF8htMFoRq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Translation contract (READ FIRST)\n2\t\n3\tWe are translating the zstd C library (in `c_src/`) to Rust, file by file, into\n4\t`src/`. The result is a `cdylib` that must export the **same symbols** and\n5\tproduce **byte-identical output** as the C build.\n6\t\n7\t## Golden rules\n8\t\n9\t1. **Transliterate, do not redesign.** Mirror the C control flow, the C\n10\t   arithmetic, the C order of operations and the C order of error checks\n11\t   *exactly*. Do NOT fix bugs. Do NOT \"improve\" anything.\n12\t2. Use **raw pointers** (`*const u8`, `*mut u32`, ...) and `unsafe` blocks so\n13\t   pointer arithmetic matches C. Do not try to use slices/iterators for the\n14\t   hot paths that do pointer arithmetic.\n15\t3. Keep **C identifiers verbatim** (`ZSTD_compressBlock_fast`, `nbSeq`, `ip`,\n16\t   `oend`, ...). Lints for naming are already disabled crate-wide.\n17\t4. **Arithmetic must wrap, never panic.** The release profile has\n18\t   `overflow-checks = false`, but be explicit where C relies on wrapping:\n19\t   use `wrapping_add/sub/mul`, and `x as i32 as u32`-style casts to mirror C\n20\t   integer conversions. Signed/unsigned conversions must match C semantics\n21\t   (C `(U32)someNegativeInt` == Rust `x as u32`).\n22\t5. For pointer subtraction that may go before the start of a buffer (common in\n23\t   zstd, e.g. `iend - 8` when the buffer is shorter), use\n24\t   `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add`/`wrapping_offset` rather than `sub`/`add`.\n25\t6. `assert()` is compiled out (DEBUGLEVEL == 0) — **drop all asserts**.\n26\t   `DEBUGLOG`/`RAWLOG`/`ZSTD_STATIC_ASSERT`/`DEBUG_STATIC_ASSERT` — drop them.\n27\t   `ZSTD_TRACE` is 0, so all `ZSTD_trace*` calls compile out.\n28\t7. Build-time configuration for this port (**already decided, do not deviate**):\n29\t   - `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT = 5`  (so `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT >= 1..5` are true,\n30\t     `>= 6`/`>= 7`/`>= 8` are false; legacy v01..v04 *source files* are still\n31\t     compiled and still export their symbols)\n32\t   - `XXH_NAMESPACE = ZSTD_`\n33\t   - `DYNAMIC_BMI2 = 0`, `STATIC_BMI2 = 0`  → always take the \"default\"\n34\t     (non-bmi2) code path; keep the `bmi2`/`flags` parameters in signatures but\n35\t     ignore them, exactly like the C does when `DYNAMIC_BMI2 == 0`.\n36\t   - `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD` is **not** defined → single-threaded `POOL_*` stubs,\n37\t     `ZSTDMT_*` compiles its non-thread paths.\n38\t   - `DEBUGLEVEL = 0`, `NDEBUG`, no\n39\t     `ZSTD_STRIP_ERROR_STRINGS`, no `HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X1/X2`,\n40\t     no `ZSTD_NO_INTRINSICS`, no `ZSTD_LINUX_KERNEL`,\n41\t     no `FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION`,\n42\t     no `ZSTD_ADDRESS_SANITIZER` / `ZSTD_MEMORY_SANITIZER`.\n43\t   - **`ZSTD_TRACE == 1`** (gcc has weak symbols) — so `ZSTD_CCtx.traceCtx` and\n44\t     `ZSTD_DCtx.traceCtx` fields **do exist** (already in the Rust structs) and\n45\t     `sizeof` depends on them. BUT the weak hooks `ZSTD_trace_compress_begin`,\n46\t     `ZSTD_trace_compress_end`, `ZSTD_trace_decompress_begin`,\n47\t     `ZSTD_trace_decompress_end` are *undefined* (NULL) in this build, so every\n48\t     `#if ZSTD_TRACE` body reduces to: set `traceCtx = 0` (the\n49\t     `(ZSTD_trace_x_begin != NULL) ? ... : 0` test is always false) and do\n50\t     nothing on end. Translate them that way — i.e. `(*cctx).traceCtx = 0;` for\n51\t     the begin hooks and nothing at all for the end hooks. Do NOT define or\n52\t     import any `ZSTD_trace_*` symbol.\n53\t   - Target is x86_64 linux (little endian, 64-bit): `MEM_64bits()==1`,\n54\t     `MEM_isLittleEndian()==1`.\n55\t   - `ZSTD_ARCH_X86_SSE2` is **not** used for `ZSTD_copy16` (gcc path uses the\n56\t     `copy16_buf` memcpy pair) — but any of these produce identical bytes.\n57\t8. **Exported symbols**: every function that the C library exports must be\n58\t   ```rust\n59\t   #[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n60\t   pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn NAME(...) -> ... { }\n61\t   ```\n62\t   with the **final linker name** (e.g. legacy files use macros that rename\n63\t   `FSE_decompress` to `FSEv05_decompress`; use the renamed name).\n64\t   `static`/internal C functions become plain (non-`no_mangle`) Rust `unsafe fn`.\n65\t   Do NOT add `no_mangle` to functions that C declared `static`.\n66\t9. Structs shared across translation units, or reachable from the public API,\n67\t   must be `#[repr(C)]`.\n68\t10. Allocation must go through libc so behaviour matches:\n69\t    `crate::libc::{malloc, calloc, free, memcpy, memmove, memset, qsort, qsort_r}`\n70\t    and the helpers `crate::libc::{ZSTD_memcpy, ZSTD_memmove, ZSTD_memset}`.\n71\t    **`qsort`/`qsort_r` must be libc's** so tie-breaking matches byte-for-byte.\n72\t11. Prefer `while` loops over `for` when translating C `for` loops with\n73\t    non-trivial increments/continues, so `continue` semantics stay correct.\n74\t    Remember: C `continue` in a `for` loop still runs the increment; Rust's does\n75\t    not.\n76\t\n77\t## Existing shared modules (use these, don't re-create them)\n78\t\n79\t| Rust path | C origin | provides |\n80\t|---|---|---|\n81\t| `crate::libc` | `zstd_deps.h` | malloc/calloc/free/memcpy/memmove/memset/memcmp/qsort/qsort_r, `ZSTD_memcpy`, `ZSTD_memmove`, `ZSTD_memset` |\n82\t| `crate::zstd_h` | `zstd.h` | all public types/enums/constants (`ZSTD_customMem`, `ZSTD_bounds`, `ZSTD_Sequence`, `ZSTD_compressionParameters`, `ZSTD_parameters`, `ZSTD_frameParameters`, `ZSTD_FrameHeader`, `ZSTD_inBuffer`, `ZSTD_outBuffer`, `ZSTD_frameProgression`, `ZSTD_strategy`, `ZSTD_cParameter`, `ZSTD_dParameter`, `ZSTD_ResetDirective`, `ZSTD_EndDirective`, `ZSTD_dictContentType_e`, `ZSTD_dictLoadMethod_e`, `ZSTD_format_e`, `ZSTD_ParamSwitch_e`, `ZSTD_dictAttachPref_e`, `ZSTD_literalCompressionMode_e`, `ZSTD_forceIgnoreChecksum_e`, `ZSTD_refMultipleDDicts_e`, `ZSTD_SequenceFormat_e`, `ZSTD_FrameType_e`, `ZSTD_nextInputType_e`