{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LYFWzq2ZLMx5ZpcvUZrhg8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* ===========================================================================\n2\t * zstd_compress.c — part 3  (C lines 2601..3630)\n3\t *\n4\t * Index rescaling, sequence-code building, entropy compression of the\n5\t * seqStore, block-compressor selection, seqStore construction, and the\n6\t * sequence-extraction API (ZSTD_generateSequences & friends).\n7\t *\n8\t * This file is `include!`d by `zstd_compress.rs`: it must contain items only,\n9\t * no `use` statements and no `extern \"C\"` blocks.\n10\t * ======================================================================== */\n11\t\n12\tpub const ZSTD_ROWSIZE: c_int = 16;\n13\t\n14\t/*! ZSTD_reduceTable() :\n15\t *  reduce table indexes by `reducerValue`, or squash to zero.\n16\t *  PreserveMark preserves \"unsorted mark\" for btlazy2 strategy.\n17\t *  It must be set to a clear 0/1 value, to remove branch during inlining.\n18\t *  Presume table size is a multiple of ZSTD_ROWSIZE\n19\t *  to help auto-vectorization */\n20\t#[inline(always)]\n21\tunsafe fn ZSTD_reduceTable_internal(\n22\t    table: *mut U32,\n23\t    size: U32,\n24\t    reducerValue: U32,\n25\t    preserveMark: c_int,\n26\t) {\n27\t    let nbRows: c_int = (size as c_int) / ZSTD_ROWSIZE;\n28\t    let mut cellNb: c_int = 0;\n29\t    let mut rowNb: c_int;\n30\t    /* Protect special index values < ZSTD_WINDOW_START_INDEX. */\n31\t    let reducerThreshold: U32 = reducerValue.wrapping_add(ZSTD_WINDOW_START_INDEX);\n32\t\n33\t    rowNb = 0;\n34\t    while rowNb < nbRows {\n35\t        let mut column: c_int = 0;\n36\t        while column < ZSTD_ROWSIZE {\n37\t            let newVal: U32;\n38\t            if preserveMark != 0 && *table.offset(cellNb as isize) == ZSTD_DUBT_UNSORTED_MARK {\n39\t                /* This write is pointless, but is required(?) for the compiler\n40\t                 * to auto-vectorize the