`, `OFFBASE_TO_REPCODE`, `ZSTD_storeSeq`, `ZSTD_storeSeqOnly`, `ZSTD_updateRep`, `ZSTD_newRep`, `ZSTD_count`, `ZSTD_count_2segments`, all `ZSTD_hash*`, `ZSTD_ipow`, `ZSTD_rollingHash_*`, all `ZSTD_window_*`, `ZSTD_matchState_dictMode`, `ZSTD_getLowestMatchIndex`, `ZSTD_getLowestPrefixIndex`, `ZSTD_index_overlap_check`, `ZSTD_writeTaggedIndex`, `ZSTD_comparePackedTags`, `ZSTD_hasExtSeqProd`, `ZSTD_BlockCompressor_f`) |\n97\t| `crate::compress::clevels` | `clevels.h` | `ZSTD_MAX_CLEVEL`, `ZSTD_defaultCParameters` |\n98\t| `crate::decompress::zstd_decompress_internal` | `zstd_decompress_internal.h` | `ZSTD_DCtx`, `ZSTD_DStream`, `ZSTD_DDict`, `ZSTD_entropyDTables_t`, `ZSTD_seqSymbol`, `ZSTD_seqSymbol_header`, `ZSTD_DDictHashSet`, `LL_base`, `OF_base`, `OF_bits`, `ML_base`, `SEQSYMBOL_TABLE_SIZE`, `ZSTD_BUILD_FSE_TABLE_WKSP_SIZE*`, `ZSTD_HUFFDTABLE_CAPACITY_LOG`, `ZSTD_LITBUFFEREXTRASIZE`, `ZSTD_DECODER_INTERNAL_BUFFER`, `ZSTDds_*`, `zdss_*`, `ZSTD_use_indefinitely`/`ZSTD_dont_use`/`ZSTD_use_once`, `ZSTD_not_in_dst`/`ZSTD_in_dst`/`ZSTD_split`, `ZSTD_DCtx_get_bmi2` |\n99\t\n100\t**Every one of the structs above has been verified to have byte-identical\n101\t`sizeof`/`align`/field offsets to the C version. Do not change their field\n102\tlists or order.**\n103\t\n104\tNote: `ZSTD_isError` / `FSE_isError` / `HUF_isError` used *inline* inside C code\n105\tare macros for `ERR_isError`. Prefer\n106\t`crate::common::error_private::ERR_isError(x) != 0`.\n107\t\n108\t## Cross-module calls\n109\t\n110\tIf module A needs a function that another module B defines, and that function is\n111\tan **exported** symbol (it appears in `SYMBOLS_BY_FILE.txt`), you may either use\n112\tthe Rust path `crate::compress::b::NAME` or declare\n113\t```rust\n114\textern \"C\" { fn NAME(args...) -> ret; }\n115\t```\n116\tPrefer the Rust path when the target module already exists; use `extern \"C\"` when\n117\tit doesn't exist yet (that keeps your file compiling independently). For C\n118\tfunctions that were `static`, they must be private to your module.\n119\t\n120\t## Verifying your work\n121\t\n122\t`./check.sh <module> [<module> ...]` type-checks the named modules together with\n123\tthe stable core, in a throw-away crate, so other people's in-progress files\n124\tcan't break your build. Module paths are relative to `src/` without `.rs`,\n125\te.g. `./check.sh compress/zstd_fast`.\n126\t\n127\t## Idioms\n128\t\n129\t```rust\n130\t// C: RETURN_ERROR_IF(cond, dstSize_tooSmall, \"...\");\n131\tif cond { return ERROR(ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall); }\n132\t\n133\t// C: FORWARD_IF_ERROR(f(...), \"\");\n134\t{ let err_code = f(...); if ERR_isError(err_code) != 0 { return err_code; } }\n135\t\n136\t// C: CHECK_F(f(...));\n137\t{ let e = f(...); if ERR_isError(e) != 0 { return e; } }\n138\t\n139\t// C: size_t const x = ...;  ->  let x: usize = ...;\n140\t// C: BYTE* op = (BYTE*)dst;  ->  let mut op = dst as *mut BYTE;\n141\t// C: op[3]                   ->  *op.add(3)\n142\t// C: *op++ = v;              ->  *op = v; op = op.add(1);\n143\t// C: (size_t)(op - ostart)   ->  op.offset_from(ostart) as usize\n144\t```\n145\t\n146\tFor a C `static const` lookup table use a Rust `static NAME: [T; N] = [...];`.\n147\t\n148\tFor C unions or nested anonymous structs, use `#[repr(C)]` structs; if a real\n149\tunion is needed use `#[repr(C)] union`.\n150\t\n151\t## Deliverable\n152\t\n153\tWrite the assigned Rust file(s) completely — **no `todo!()`, no stubs, no\n154\t\"... rest omitted\"**. Every function in the assigned C file must be present.\n155\tDo not edit anything under `c_src/`. Do not edit `src/lib.rs` unless told to.\n156\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LsmnNuEGEHszt1SKmZB1Xm","session_id":"91081e33-7aae-4a44-80fe-383759459deb","uuid":"9ff57518-0cd9-43ec-b3a0-d4644b454b47","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:59:07.178Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate zdict"}
